    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11.1">
        <head>Cn 1018 11.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#kennedy" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="75" ed="#kennedy"/>And ealle godes þeowas we biddað 7 lǽrað. 7 huruþinga sacerdas. <hi rend="italic">þæt</hi> hi gode hiran 7 clænnesse lufian. 7 beorgan him silfum wið godes irre. 7 wið ðone weallendan bryne þe wealleð on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="214" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ealle Godes þeowas we biddað and lærað, and huruþinga sacerdas, þæt hi Gode hiran and clænnesse lufian and beorgan him silfum wið Godes irre and wið ðone weallendan bryne, þe wealleð on helle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#kennedy" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="75" ed="#kennedy"/>And we bid and instruct all the servants of God, and especially priests, that they obey God and love celibacy, and protect themselves against the raging fire that blazes in hell.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="215" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we require and instruct that all servants of God, especially priests, obey God, embrace celibacy, and protect themselves against the burning fire that rages in hell.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_41">VI Atr 41</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><ref target="clause:ICn_6-1">I Cn 6.1–2a</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Kennedy n. 74: þæt: MS 7.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt hi: and hi D</note>
      </div>
    </body>
